# Normalize line endings on checkout, whatever core.autocrlf is set to on the machine.
#
# The repository stores LF. The raw strings inside js/prompts-data.js hold their line
# breaks as JSON escape sequences rather than as real newlines, so git never rewrites
# them. Without this file, a checkout on a machine with core.autocrlf=true produces
# CRLF source files under prompts/ while their mirrored copies stay LF, and the two
# stop matching byte for byte even though nothing is wrong.
#
# That is the project's central invariant, so the fix belongs here rather than in each
# tool that reads these files. See docs/PRD.md section 19, question 5.

* text=auto eol=lf
